        "q2": "<div style='background-color: #f1f2f6; border-left: 5px solid #00cec9; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><strong style='display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 5px;'>Part 2: Questions 11-20</strong><span style='font-size: 0.9rem; color: #57606f;'>Questions 11-16: Choose the correct letter, <strong>A, B or C</strong>.</span></div><h3 style='color: #2f3542; text-align: center; font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 20px;'>BECOMING A MILLIONAIRE</h3><div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 30px;'><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>11</span> 11. Arthur feels that when starting a business, mistakes should be</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-11' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='11'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> seen as an opportunity to learn.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> predicted and minimised.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> avoided at all costs.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>12</span> 12. Recent American studies found that confidence will</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-12' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='12'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> sometimes reduce people's chances of success.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> be increased by reading self-help books.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> ensure good results on business courses.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>13</span> 13. The American studies recommended that new entrepreneurs</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-13' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='13'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> listen to their colleagues' advice.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> get professional help when things go wrong.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> remain concentrated on their aims.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>14</span> 14. What does Arthur say about his own experience of marketing?</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-14' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='14'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> He relied on what he already knew.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> He hired an expert to take care of it.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> He realised its importance too late.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>15</span> 15. What does Arthur think is an important quality shared by good leaders?</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-15' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='15'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> They are ambitious for their company.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> They can deal with difficult people.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> They earn the respect of their workforce.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>16</span> 16. What does Arthur say about taking risks?</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-16' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='16'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> He advises being cautious.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> He favours a long-term view.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> He believes it is financially advantageous.</span></div></div></div></div><div style='background-color: #f1f2f6; border-left: 5px solid #00cec9; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 25px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><strong style='display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 5px;